      proofName: "Valuations of the elementary symmetric functions",
      formula: String.raw`\text{slope } -\lambda \ \text{of length}\ \ell \;\Rightarrow\; \#\{ i : v(\alpha_i) = \lambda \} = \ell`,
      text: "Over a field complete for a valuation v, if the Newton polygon of f has a segment of slope −λ and horizontal length ℓ, then f has exactly ℓ roots of valuation λ in a splitting field, and f factors over K accordingly, one factor for each segment.",
